  1672.7 ? outLamp4=on outLamp5=on outLamp6=on  "a. Move slide switch 6 to the LEFT. | b. Enter the larger number (7) by pushing pushbutton 6 the correct number of times. The counter is now displaying the larger number. | 1 | NO | 1 | NO | 1 | UP | 7 | the low order flip-flop (represented by light 6) changes each time the pushbutton is pushed and released. The low order flip-flop represents 1's (units). The next flip-flop to the left (represented by light 5) changes every other time the pushbutton is pushed and released. This flip-flop represents 2's. And of course, the high order flip-flop (represented by light 4) changes every fourth time the pushbutton is pushed and released; the high order flip-flop thus represents 4's. | Light 4 | FLIP-FLOP A | Light 5 | FLIP-FLOP B | Light 6 | FLIP-FLOP C | Binary output lights 4, 5 and 6 will read OFF, OFF, ON or 001. The Binary Counter is displaying a 1."
